{:edb/db-before-t 2837 :edb/db-after-t 2838 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536150 50 #inst "2026-10-09T17:08:19.778Z" 13194139536150 true] [17592186100650 1100 "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" 13194139536150 true] [17592186100650 1100 "The graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[1,6],$ is shown below. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $5$ and $2,$ respectively (from left to right). Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[1,6].$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/6433d1ca57ceb334f304e894e2655ef50d987567fbcf219314302bb381fd9a83.png)" 13194139536150 false] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386149 13194139536150 true] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386156 13194139536150 true] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386177 13194139536150 true] [17592186100934 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386184 13194139536150 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386191 13194139536150 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386198 13194139536150 true] [17592186100935 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386205 13194139536150 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386163 13194139536150 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386212 13194139536150 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386217 13194139536150 true] [17592186100936 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386224 13194139536150 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386170 13194139536150 true] [17592186100937 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386231 13194139536150 true] [17592186101252 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536150 true] [17592186101252 1100 "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=3{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[-2,2].$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186101252 1100 "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x) = 3x^{2}$ on the interval $[- 2, 2]$." 13194139536150 false] [17592186101252 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot ({x}^{3})|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[{2}^{3}-(-2)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4 \\\\ 3{c}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ c & =\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186291203 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186291203 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013500/assets/64682c2166e3f9fd2366f925330d04f95b54f370fd3d887d1d8aef8885ac35ec.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-8,4],$ is shown above. The areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $20$, $80$ and $10,$ respectively (from left to right). \n\nFind the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,4].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{fi