e] [17592186386149 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386150 13194139536150 true] [17592186386149 1089 "q-120298" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386149 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536150 true] [17592186386149 1100 "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=6{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[-1,2].$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386149 1113 #uuid "eef23b72-e36a-5c45-a5b3-e03a1d351b74" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386149 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-1)}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (2{x}^{3})|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[2(2)^{3}-2(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =6 \\\\ 6{c}^{2} & =6 \\\\ {c}^{2} & =1 \\\\ c & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386151 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386152 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386153 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386154 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386155 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1041 "selection" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386152 13194139536150 true] [17592186386150 1110 #uuid "6d01f545-648e-544e-bd81-bf3ed51943fe" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386151 1034 "\\pm \\sqrt{6}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386151 1111 #uuid "a711b4cd-449a-5b67-bc2b-1daf47ab2a29" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386152 1034 "\\pm 1" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386152 1111 #uuid "e4f4344c-5821-5448-bbf8-caf063e16d8b" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386153 1034 "1" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386153 1111 #uuid "8bc5d772-308a-5e43-9c75-bbf99a23b44c" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386154 1034 "\\pm 6" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386154 1111 #uuid "f077af58-34cf-5d08-95a9-5150fb89c66b" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386155 1034 "-1" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386155 1111 #uuid "78473b4c-b515-5fd8-8166-4e008255ff46" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386156 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386157 13194139536150 true] [17592186386156 1089 "q-120333" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386156 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536150 true] [17592186386156 1100 "Find all values of $c$ that satisfy the mean value theorem for integrals for  $f(x)=5\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}$ on the interval $[0,2].$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386156 1113 #uuid "e2b64626-04c3-5fb9-a70b-3ec150e19575" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386156 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-0}{\\int }_{0}^{2}5\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2{x}^{5/2})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[2\\cdot {2}^{5/2}-2\\cdot {0}^{5/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 5\\sqrt{{c}^{3}} & =4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386158 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386159 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386160 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386161 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386162 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1041 "selection" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386158 13194139536150 true] [17592186386157 1110 #uuid "fdcd021c-11f6-5e32-90b2-c5143d5dbd98" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386158 1034 "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{32}{25}}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386158 1111 #uuid "3d9bf282-58a1-5d82-b0e7-c72fdf9d90e5" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386159 1034 "\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{16}{5}}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386159 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386159 1111 #uuid "41901d4d-81c2-562f-abe2-33e08b75c0e2" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386160 1034 "\\frac{32}{25}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386160 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386160 1111 #uuid "81d09b30-d0f9-5648-a9dd-72ef95d21227" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386161 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386161 1111 #uuid "e3a3cd76-835c-5485-b247-c563ad07c69f" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386162 1034 "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{25}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386162 1111 #uuid "2b3323d0-b849-5ade-bdce-8dad4c76f1da" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386163 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386164 13194139536150 true] [17592186386163 1089 "q-120450" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386163 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536150 true] [17592186386163 1100 "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-9{x}^{2}+14x-2$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386163 1113 #uuid "645765fa-26ae-5ed8-a0d8-99efa4f8225a" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386163 1145 "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-9{x}^{2}+14x-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-3{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-3{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-2c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-3{c}^{2}+7c-2 \\\\ 3{c}^{2}-7c+2 & =0 \\\\ (c-2)(3c-1) & =0 \\\\ c & =2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386165 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386166 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386167 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386168 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386169 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1041 "selection" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386167 13194139536150 true] [17592186386164 1110 #uuid "61d61f9f-b9eb-5c9d-8c61-aefcbb45c2a0" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386165 1034 "0,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386165 1111 #uuid "5e3208c6-746e-5199-90ad-789d0a4b2409" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386166 1034 "-2,\\,3" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386166 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386166 1111 #uuid "ef74a6b0-7f25-544b-b8ae-f7d47395dabf" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386167 1034 "2,\\,\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386167 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386167 1111 #uuid "b7cc8716-b4a7-5334-9599-1a521a91bffa" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386168 1034 "\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386168 1111 #uuid "e91cd08b-ba6d-527f-b8ad-1b84c3416576" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386169 1034 "-3,\\,2" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386169 1111 #uuid "88809e12-686d-52c1-966f-b7ab0228f703" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386170 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386171 13194139536150 true] [17592186386170 1089 "q-18143" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386170 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536150 true] [17592186386170 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081209/assets/7eddb6203ccc3eead9a2a89d7868d3206af52be4c269962e33c551ddd3cf08cd.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-4,4],$ is shown above. It consists of six line segments.  Find the average value of $f(x)$ on $[-1,3].$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386170 1113 #uuid "fbfdded4-c230-5698-b4cd-d1a52f9642db" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386170 1145 "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3-(-1)}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386172 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386173 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386174 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386175 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386176 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1041 "selection" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386175 13194139536150 true] [17592186386171 1110 #uuid "c99991c4-91d3-56e9-86a4-3e7f15632f3e" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386172 1034 "\\frac{7}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386172 1111 #uuid "404e9f9c-aace-5a13-85bf-68c2cfbc6896" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386173 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386173 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386173 1111 #uuid "ea863b2c-2f4f-59f2-aa56-01a4f179ef4d" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386174 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386174 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386174 1111 #uuid "bc641657-f01d-5448-868b-b2f2e9979abd" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386175 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386175 1111 #uuid "cb4f1599-3de3-5096-9d83-500f1b467fe8" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386176 1034 "\\frac{5}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386176 1111 #uuid "e564d2b2-f995-5714-b7c9-a3a83e4f5605" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386177 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386178 13194139536150 true] [17592186386177 1089 "q-2474" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386177 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536150 true] [17592186386177 1100 "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=-x+2$ on the interval $[-2,2].$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386177 1113 #uuid "c4b62ed1-12e5-5a6e-aad0-bc0c6b0adfd0" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386177 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals. we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}(-x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2x)|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}+2\\cdot 2)-(-\\frac{(-2)^{2}}{2}+2\\cdot (-2))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[2-(-6)] \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =2 \\\\ -c+2 & =2 \\\\ c & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386179 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386180 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386181 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386182 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386183 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1041 "selection" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386183 13194139536150 true] [17592186386178 1110 #uuid "5212c4b8-99cc-5faa-87db-05ad7d8c8963" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386179 1034 "\\pm 1" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386179 1111 #uuid "9de014ad-2055-5349-9244-64ad84e18e91" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386180 1034 "2" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386180 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386180 1111 #uuid "e3abe82d-e288-51a6-a112-e9d1b2bc0aaa" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386181 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386181 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386181 1111 #uuid "a85a5c86-d002-5709-9803-6467b782f27a" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386182 1034 "4" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386182 1111 #uuid "1413b167-c304-5d75-a8ed-cab2474cc2f8" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386183 1034 "0" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386183 1111 #uuid "d9799a52-0244-5aec-b5ca-0ebcd18def1b" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386184 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386185 13194139536150 true] [17592186386184 1089 "q-2476" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386184 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536150 true] [17592186386184 1100 "Find the value of $c$ that satisfies the mean value theorem for integrals for $f(x)=4+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}$ on the interval $[1,2].$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386184 1113 #uuid "861d7909-aecf-5978-9bba-b5634c19846a" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386184 1145 "Applying the mean value theorem for the integrals, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c)(b-a) & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ f(c) & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(4+\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(4x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2-\\frac{1}{{2}^{2}})-(4\\cdot 1-\\frac{1}{{1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{4}-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the expression for $f(x)$ to solve for the value of $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(c) & =\\frac{19}{4} \\\\ 4+\\frac{2}{{c}^{3}} & =\\frac{19}{4} \\\\ \\frac{2}{{c}^{3}} & =\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{{c}^{3}}{2} & =\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ {c}^{3} & =\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ c & =\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{8}{3}} \\\\ c & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386186 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386187 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386188 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386189 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386190 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1041 "selection" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386187 13194139536150 true] [17592186386185 1110 #uuid "dce538c8-a1b8-5237-b33b-7e091e8514e5" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386186 1034 "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386186 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386186 1111 #uuid "7561c120-2dd2-5147-a914-b9d8055b13e5" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386187 1034 "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{3}}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386187 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386187 1111 #uuid "87172de7-e0a9-5165-8750-ad28138c18b7" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386188 1034 "\\sqrt[3]{2}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386188 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386188 1111 #uuid "0c224cc2-de66-57d2-b97a-b6ee32f04489" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386189 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386189 1111 #uuid "2b4da1d6-8785-5852-983c-273d5447277e" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386190 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386190 1111 #uuid "d89224a4-7338-5554-b49a-7e20f0f12bd8" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386191 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386192 13194139536150 true] [17592186386191 1089 "q-30771" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386191 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536150 true] [17592186386191 1100 "Find the average value of the function $f(x)={x}^{3}-2x$ on the interval $[-2,1].$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386191 1113 #uuid "21ad90ae-5ee1-51ed-8041-81806b6326c8" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386191 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(-2)}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{1}({x}^{3}-2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}-{x}^{2})|}_{-2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {1}^{4}-{1}^{2})-(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot (-2)^{4}-(-2)^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{3}{4}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386193 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386194 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386195 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386196 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386197 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1041 "selection" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386197 13194139536150 true] [17592186386192 1110 #uuid "65f4a48a-0645-5349-9e19-34bf740f062b" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386193 1034 "-\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386193 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386193 1111 #uuid "2285b351-3144-5af3-8c46-2b7da81a7ca4" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386194 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386194 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386194 1111 #uuid "ec7de4e6-1c18-5e63-954f-1af030a0a984" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386195 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386195 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386195 1111 #uuid "ce5891c3-61a1-5005-9fa6-f33121a7766d" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386196 1034 "0" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386196 1111 #uuid "5486a4db-79dd-5af5-92ca-4cf84540f79f" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386197 1034 "-\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386197 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536150 true] [17592186386197 1111 #uuid "0475e6ab-edab-5c23-bf18-ca5014dabcec" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386198 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386199 13194139536150 true] [17592186386198 1089 "q-30893" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386198 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536150 true] [17592186386198 1100 "Within the interval $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ determine the average value of $g(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386198 1113 #uuid "c8da72f4-4be3-59c9-b893-26555f51f2de" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386198 1145 "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\frac{\\pi }{2}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{\\pi }(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)|}_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2}))+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{2})))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }[(0+(-1))-(0+1)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3\\pi }(-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536150 true] [17592186386199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386200 13194139536150 true] [17592186386199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386201 13194139536150 true] [17592186386199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386202 13194139536150 true] [17592186386199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386203 13194139536150 true] [17592186386199 1000 #edb/ref 1